  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z=6 \\\\ y-9z=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-2$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $6$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z=6 \\\\ 0x+y-9z=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
